//! user/install/sudogroup.lu — the installer's user in group sudo (px106, R-px106-6: B3, Ubuntu's own
//! shape: `%sudo ALL=(ALL:ALL) ALL` in /etc/sudoers, group `sudo` at gid 27, the installer's user a
//! member, so `id` shows `27(sudo)` and a second administrator is added as on Ubuntu, by adding them
//! to the group).
//!
//! `sudo_member(text, name)` is /etc/group's text with `name` a member of `sudo`, every other line
//! byte for byte: no `sudo` line, `sudo:x:27:NAME` appended; a `sudo` line at gid 27 without them,
//! them added at the end of its member list; already a member, the text unchanged. Refused by name,
//! the file being the user's: gid 27 held by a group not named `sudo` (`gid_taken`), and a `sudo` line
//! at another gid (`sudo_gid`). The fresh install (prepare.lu) and the upgrade (upgrade.lu) both use it.

/// Rows first (px106): this answers the text unchanged until the change is written.
fn sudo_member(text: str, name: str) -> str ! {gid_taken, sudo_gid} {
    text
}
